hadiths[24]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1524","**Muhammad ibn 'Ubayd al-Muharibi al-Kufi narrated to us, saying:** Sharik narrated to us, from Abu al-Hasna', from al-Hakam, from Hanish, from 'Ali رضي الله عنه, that he used to offer two rams as a sacrifice (udhiyah): one on behalf of the Prophet ﷺ and the other on behalf of himself. When he was asked about this, he said: **\He commanded me to do so\""** — meaning the Prophet ﷺ — **\""and I shall never abandon it.\""**\n\nAbu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: **\""This is a gharib (uncommon) Hadith. We do not know it except through the narration of Sharik.\""**\n\nHe further stated: **\""Some of the people of knowledge have permitted that a sacrifice be offered on behalf of the deceased"
"1525","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:\I attended the Eid Al-Adha' with the Prophet (ﷺ) at the Musalla. When he finished his Khutbah"""
"1526","Narrated by al-Bara' ibn 'Azib (may Allah be pleased with him), who reported that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said:\n\n\One should not sacrifice a lame animal whose lameness is apparent"
"1527","he should be given a name, and his head should be shaved. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1522 Arabic Hadees: 1522\""
1528"""
"1528","Al-Hasan ibn 'Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Sharik ibn 'Abdullah informed us from Abu Ishaq, from Shurayh ibn al-Nu'man al-Sa'idi, who is al-Hamdani, from 'Ali ibn Abi Talib, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to examine the eye and ear (of the sacrificial animal), and not to sacrifice one with muqabalah, mudabarah, sharqa', or kharqa'."
"1529","Narrated 'Aishah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \There is no vowing for disobedience"""
"1530","Narrated 'Aishah:That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \There is no vowing in disobedience to Allah"""
"1531","Narrated Thabit bin Adh-Dahhak:That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \It is not for a person to vow about that over which he has no control"""
"1532","Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \The atonement of a vow when it is not specified is the atonement of an oath"""
"1533","Narrated 'Abdur-Rahman bin Samurah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \O 'Abdur-Rahman! Do not ask for a position of leadership"""
"1534","Narrated Abu Hurairah:That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Whoever takes an oath"""
"1535","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever swears about an oath and says: 'If Allah wills (Insha Allah)"""
"1536","Narrated Abu Hurairah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever swears [about an oath] and says: 'If Allah wills (Insha Allah)"""
"1537","Narrated Salim:From his father (Ibn 'Umar) that the Prophet (ﷺ) heard 'Umar saying: \By my father"""
"1538","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) came across 'Umar while he was on his mount"
"1539","Narrated Sa'd bin 'Ubaidah:That Ibn 'Umar heard a man saying: \No by the Ka'bah\"" so Ibn 'Umar said: \""Nothing is sworn by other than Allah"""
"1540","**Narrated by al-Bara' ibn 'Azib (may Allah be pleased with him):**\n\nHe said: \The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) addressed us on the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Nahr) and said: **'None of you should slaughter until he has prayed.'**\n\nSo my maternal uncle stood up and said: 'O Messenger of Allah"
"1541","Narrated Abu Hurairah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Do not vow"""
"1542","Narrated 'Umar:\I said:'O Messenger of Allah! I had vowed to perform I'tikaf in Al-Masjid Al-Haram for a night during the era of Jahiliyyah.' He said: 'Fulfill your vow"""
"1543","Narrated Salim bin 'Abdullah:From this father (Ibn Umar) who said: \The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) often would swear with this oath: 'No! By the Changer of the Hearts"""
"1544","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) saying: 'Whoever frees a believing slave"""
"1545","Narrated Suwaid bin Muqarrin Al-Muzani:\We were seven brothers without a servant except one"""
"1546","Narrated Thabit bin Adh-Dahhak:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever swears by a religion other than Islam while lying"""
"1547","Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir:\I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! My sister vowed that she would walk to the House barefoot and without Khimar (covering).' The Prophet (ﷺ) said: 'Verily Allah will not do anything with the misery of your sister. She should ride"""
